---
title: "Command Dispatch Flow (TCP path)"
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant CC as Claude Code
    participant MCP as MCP Server<br/>(Python 3.14)
    participant TCP as TCP 9877
    participant RS as Remote Script<br/>(Python 3.11)
    participant REG as _registry
    participant H as Handler
    participant LOM as Live Object Model

    CC->>MCP: tool call (stdio)
    activate MCP
    Note over MCP: @mcp.tool() validates args<br/>@_tool_handler acquires semaphore

    MCP->>MCP: Build cmd_params: CreateClipAutomationParams<br/>(TypedDict — static analysis)
    MCP->>TCP: send_command("create_clip_automation", params)
    activate TCP
    TCP->>RS: {"type": "create_clip_automation", "params": {...}}\n
    activate RS

    RS->>RS: _process_command()<br/>command_type in get_modifying_commands()?

    RS->>RS: schedule_message(0, task)<br/>→ queued for Ableton main thread

    Note over RS: Main thread picks up task

    RS->>REG: dispatch("create_clip_automation", song, params, ctrl)
    activate REG
    REG->>REG: Lookup _REGISTRY["create_clip_automation"]<br/>Introspect param specs from @command
    REG->>REG: Build kwargs from params_dict<br/>using function signature defaults

    REG->>H: create_clip_automation(song, track_index=0, ...)
    activate H
    H->>LOM: clip.automation_envelope(param)
    LOM-->>H: envelope
    H->>LOM: envelope.insert_step(time, 0.001, value)
    LOM-->>H: ok
    H-->>REG: {"parameter": "Volume", "points_added": 42}
    deactivate H

    REG-->>RS: result dict
    deactivate REG

    RS-->>TCP: {"status": "success", "result": {...}}\n
    deactivate RS
    TCP-->>MCP: JSON response
    deactivate TCP

    MCP-->>CC: tool result string
    deactivate MCP
